       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.     TR3PURCH.
       AUTHOR.         CA YODER.
       DATE-WRITTEN.   OCTOBER 1998.
       DATE-COMPILED.

      ************************************************************
      **                                                        **
      ** TR3PURCH                                               **
      ** ========                                               **
      **   THIS PROGRAM EXTRACTS CSIS PURCHASING DATA FOR R/3.  **
      **                                                        **
      ** FILES CREATED:                                         **
      ** ==============                                         **
      **   R3BLANKET   --  BLANKET ORDER HEADER/ITEM INFO       **
      **   R3CONTRACT  --  LOCAL CONTRACT (REQMT ORDER)  INFO   **
      **   R3PURCH     --  PURCHASE ORDERS & RELEASES           **
      **   R3UNCLASS   --  UNCLASSIFIED PURCHASE ORDERS         **
      **                                                        **
      ************************************************************
      ** 12/18/2003   BRUCE GEISER     (JEAN CHASE REQUEST)     **
      **  FORCED FRAMEWORK ORDERS TO TYPE FO, FORCED STANDARD   **
      **  ORDERS TO TYPE NB, MADE ALL FO ORDERS CATEGORY B.     **
      **  CHANGED PO CUTOFF DATES FROM 1998 TO 2003.            **
      **                                                        **
      ** 01/19/2004   BRUCE GEISER     (JEAN CHASE REQUEST)     **
      **  SKIP PO'S FROM CORPORATE, THESE ALREADY EXIST IN SAP  **
      **  IF PO HEADER COMPANY DOES NOT MATCH PLANT CODE - SKIP **
      **                                                        **
      ** 02/09/2004   BRUCE GEISER     (JEAN CHASE REQUEST)     **
      **  ADD TRAILING ZERO TO ITEM NUM. USE 20040101 FOR EXPIRE**
      **  DATE CHECK ON REQUIREMENT ORDERS. CHANGE CATAGORY OF  **
      **  CONSIGNMENT ITEMS TO "K".                             **
      **                                                        **
      ** 02/17/2004   BRUCE GEISER     (ALL PLANTS REQUEST)     **
      **  SKIP REPAIR ORDER ITEMS WITH ZERO QUANTITY AND PRICE. **
      **                                                        **
      ** 02/2004      HARRY PROCTOR                             **
      **    Added byte to Plant ID Table for Ariba PO           **
      **  indicator.  Populated field and added logic to        **
      **  identify Ariba originated orders.                     **
      **    Created 01 STATUS-FLAGS to hold 88 level switches.  **
      **  Made one switch name OPEN-PO-SW and commented out     **
      **  the 77 level variable OPEN-PO-SW so all existing      **
      **  logic continues to function the same.  New logic uses **
      **  88 level switch OPEN-ORDER.                           **
      **    Added logic to skip PO's if they are a Repair PO    **
      **  and the Qty and Price are Zero and skip POs if they   **
      **  originated in Ariba and the Qty is Zero. (Ref para    **
      **  922-CHECK-OPEN-PO) Also added 2 accumulators so all   **
      **  items are checked on the PO.                          **
      **    Added logic to para 830-Write-Items to not write    **
      **  Item records if the item is closed.                   **
      **                                                        **
      ** 04/07/2004   BRUCE GEISER                              **
      **  UPDATE REPAIR AND ARIBA OPEN ORDER SELECTION LOGIC.   **
      **  SKIP ALL ITEM OUTPUT LOGIC IF ITEM CLOSED.            **
      **  REMOVED BUDGET CHECKS, USER CAN MODIFY TO ANY AMOUNT. **
      **                                                        **
      ** 04/15/2004   Harry Proctor                             **
      **  Modified logic for Purchase Order processing to       **
      **  inhibit the writing of Header records unless or       **
      **  until a detail item record is to be written.          **
      **                                                        **
      ** 05/03/2004   Harry Proctor                             **
      **  Ariba is sending display control characters as part   **
      **  of the Text fields on PO Records.  Added Para 999-    **
      **  to scan Text fields and replace these control chars   **
      **  with an asterisk (*) before sending to SAP.           **
      **                                                        **
      ** 05/13/2004   Harry Proctor                             **
      **  Modified 902- to pass the last 3 characters of the    **
      **  PO record Accounting Information field as characters  **
      **  7 thru 9 of the Accounting Number field being passed  **
      **  to SAP.  They could not convert the Expense Class     **
      **  that was being passed to an Expense Code and found    **
      **  these 3 characters in the PO record are the Expense   **
      **  Code.                                                 **
      **       Also modified the New Work logic to move a       **
      **  constant of "250" to the Class field if the order is  **
      **  a New Work order.                                     **
      **                                                        **
      ** 05/19/2004   Harry Proctor                             **
      **  Added Initialize to reset out bound records before    **
      **  processing a new PO.                                  **
      **      Changed calculation of OVERALL-LIMIT to use QTY   **
      **  * PRICE if both are > zero, otherwise use BUDGET      **
      **  from PO Header but adjust for multiple items and those *
      **  that have valid QTY and PRICE.                        **
      **      Added INSPECT logic to find Contract and Purchase **
      **  orders that have incomplete accounting information    **
      **  by looking for spaces in the records being passed to  **
      **  SAP.                                                  **
      **                                                        **
      ** 05/26/2004   BRUCE GEISER                              **
      **  TWEAKED THE ACCOUNT NUMBER FIELD FOR SALLY.           **
      **                                                        **
      ** 06/28/2004   BRUCE GEISER                              **
      **  INCLUDED INTERNAL TRANSFER ORDERS IN LOAD FOR SALLY.  **
      **  FORCED BUYER TO BE 'STO' ON IT'S.                     **
      **                                                        **
      ************************************************************

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.

       SOURCE-COMPUTER.          IBM-AS400.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER.          IBM-AS400.
         SPECIAL-NAMES.   LOCAL-DATA IS LDA
                          C01 IS PAGE-EJECT.

       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT MSTORERM-I
               ASSIGN         TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0201
               ORGANIZATION   IS INDEXED
                 ACCESS MODE  IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY     IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS    IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MPLTINFO-I
               ASSIGN         TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0501
               ORGANIZATION   IS INDEXED
               ACCESS MODE    IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY     IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS    IS FILE-STATUS.

      *--------- CHANGED LOGICAL FILE SO THAT PURCHASE ORDERS ARE
      *--------- IN ORDER BY BUYER CODE.
           SELECT DPORECD-I
               ASSIGN         TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0905
               ORGANIZATION   IS INDEXED
               ACCESS MODE    IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY     IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                 WITH DUPLICATES
               FILE STATUS    IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DPOITEM-I
               ASSIGN         TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1002
               ORGANIZATION   IS INDEXED
               ACCESS MODE    IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY     IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                 WITH DUPLICATES
               FILE STATUS    IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DPODATAITM-I
               ASSIGN         TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1101
               ORGANIZATION   IS INDEXED
               ACCESS MODE    IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY     IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                 WITH DUPLICATES
               FILE STATUS    IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DCOMMENT-I
               ASSIGN         TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1901
               ORGANIZATION   IS INDEXED
               ACCESS MODE    IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY     IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                 WITH DUPLICATES
               FILE STATUS    IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DINVRCD-I
               ASSIGN         TO DATABASE-MCFLCS2502
               ORGANIZATION   IS INDEXED
               ACCESS MODE    IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY     IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                 WITH DUPLICATES
               FILE STATUS    IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DINVITM-I
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS2601
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                 ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                 WITH DUPLICATES
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MVALIDPLTDATA-I
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1701
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                  ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT BLANKET-FILE
               ASSIGN TO DISK-R3BLANKET.

           SELECT CONTRACT-FILE
               ASSIGN TO DISK-R3CONTRACT.

           SELECT PURCH-FILE
               ASSIGN TO DISK-R3PURCH.

           SELECT INSTR-FILE
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-R3STDINST.

           SELECT UNCLASS-FILE
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-R3UNCLASS.

           SELECT PRINT-FILE  ASSIGN TO PRINTER-MCPRT.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD  MSTORERM-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MSTORERM-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS  OF MCFLCS0201.

       FD  MPLTINFO-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MPLTINFO-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0500  OF MCFLCS0501.

       FD  DPORECD-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DPORECD-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLCS0905.

       FD  DPOITEM-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DPOITEM-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS1000  OF MCFLCS1002.

       FD  DPODATAITM-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DPODATAITM-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS  OF MCFLCS1101.

       FD  DCOMMENT-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DCOMMENT-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS  OF MCFLCS1901.

       FD  DINVRCD-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DINVRCD-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLCS2502.

       FD  DINVITM-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DINVITM-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS2600  OF MCFLCS2601.

       FD  MVALIDPLTDATA-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MVALIDPLTDATA-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLCS1701.

       FD  BLANKET-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED
           RECORD CONTAINS 266 CHARACTERS
           DATA RECORD IS BLANKET-REC.
       01  BLANKET-REC               PIC X(266).

       FD  CONTRACT-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED
           RECORD CONTAINS 266 CHARACTERS
           DATA RECORD IS CONTRACT-REC.
       01  CONTRACT-REC              PIC X(266).

       FD  PURCH-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED
           RECORD CONTAINS 266 CHARACTERS
           DATA RECORD IS PURCH-REC.
       01  PURCH-REC                 PIC X(266).

       FD  INSTR-FILE
           DATA RECORD IS INSTR-REC
           RECORD CONTAINS 3 CHARACTERS
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  INSTR-REC                  PIC X(3).

       FD  UNCLASS-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED
           RECORD CONTAINS 266 CHARACTERS
           DATA RECORD IS UNCLASS-REC.
       01  UNCLASS-REC                 PIC X(266).

       FD  PRINT-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED
           RECORD CONTAINS 132 CHARACTERS
           DATA RECORD IS PRINT-REC.
       01  PRINT-REC                     PIC X(132).

